  "path": "concepts/evidence-receipt-qualification.md",
  "title": "Evidence receipts must separate integrity, qualification, and execution",
  "body": "# Evidence receipts must separate integrity, qualification, and execution\n\nA passing receipt verifies only the claims it explicitly measures. Record these dimensions separately:\n\n- **Integrity:** hashes, sizes, schema checks, reproducibility, and receipt consistency.\n- **Qualification:** which sources, observations, dates, and capabilities were actually available and supported.\n- **Execution scope:** offline fixture, historical simulation, native provider call, paper trading, or production execution.\n\nDo not promote a receipt that passes integrity checks into a claim of complete source coverage, profitable strategy behavior, live-market validity, broker execution, or unattended production readiness. Preserve unsupported and unavailable-source statuses in the receipt so later reviewers can distinguish a bounded result from a complete qualification.",
