{
  "path": "gotchas/prompt-cache-is-not-token-savings.md",
  "title": "Prompt-cache share is not the same as net token savings",
  "body": "# Prompt-cache share is not the same as net token savings\n\nA high cached-input percentage describes how provider accounting classified input; it does not by itself demonstrate lower total tokens, lower cost, shorter prompts, or better task efficiency.\n\nWhen evaluating caching, compare a frozen task under equivalent uncached and cached conditions and report at least:\n\n- total input, cached input, output, and total tokens;\n- request count and repeated-context size;\n- latency and failure/retry behavior; and\n- the provider's billing treatment of cached tokens.\n\nUse the measured baseline and the controlled comparison, not cache share alone, to claim savings.",
